# Git default branch

When initializing git repositories or creating GitHub repos for this project, always use `main` as the default branch name, never `master`.

- Run `git init -b main` (or set `init.defaultBranch` before init) so the first branch is `main`
- When creating GitHub repos with `gh repo create`, ensure the default branch is `main`
- If a repo was created with `master`, rename locally with `git branch -m master main`, push `main`, set it as the default on GitHub, then delete `master` on the remote
